@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+# Trade For acquisition costs — build 2251
+
+## Confirmed gap and narrow correction
+
+The bounded search already constrains the exact target and sends each candidate
+through the shared bilateral evaluator. Its result display previously sorted by
+existing strategy, collapsed equivalent pick constructions, preferred package
+shapes, then truncated to three. Both steps could remove the least expensive
+eligible assessed offer. The prior `offer_level` label was not rendered by the
+shared offer card.
+
+The existing strategy and saved soft-preference order now establishes the fit
+leader before presentation pruning. A request-local presentation selector also
+retains the minimum fully evidenced **gross outgoing Neutral Market** package
+among the eligible assessments from that same search. Both anchors survive the
+existing shape/equivalent-pick diversity selection. A shared anchor appears once.
+Existing relative order resolves exact cost ties without display rounding. At
+most three cards remain; no discovery, evaluation or repair budget is enlarged.
+
+## Evidence contract
+
+Prices must match the shared canonical Market balance admitted in each completed
+evaluation and its current request's neutral asset pool. Full compatible prices
+on both sides, valid exact identities and canonical ownership are required for
+cost selection. Missing, partial, nonfinite, negative, incompatible-unit,
+changed-price or ambiguous pick evidence cannot win cost selection. Zero remains
+zero. A missing cost never removes a separately eligible assessed offer; its cost
+is unknown. Incoming extras and net received-minus-sent are separate, using the
+same canonical package arithmetic. Different extras are not equivalent purchases.
+
+Custom construction and evaluation preserve their existing saved method,
+revision, scope and prices. Cost selection uses the preserved neutral pools and
+neutral evaluator evidence, never personal slot values. Same-search source
+boundary and ownership rechecks remain in place. No retained offer is reranked
+against a later inventory or quote. Existing stale/retained and comparison
+admission checks govern read-only previews and reload/Back.
+
+Cost roles are descriptions within a limited search, not global optima, manager
+asking prices, acceptance promises, new recommendation tiers or valuations.
+FAIR / OPTIONAL remains optional, and cheaper rejected/evidence-limited offers
+remain outside eligible results. Exact target, original-franchise picks,
+protections and exclusions remain enforced by the existing search and evaluator.
+
+## Scope and verification
+
+`services/trade_for_acquisition.py` selects from existing evaluated results;
+`services/trade_intelligence.py` invokes it at the presentation boundary. The
+released workspace/comparison JavaScript renders and retains the compact record
+inside existing bounded, account/league/franchise-scoped state. Existing decision,
+production, reserve, roster-space and future-capital disclosures are reused.
+Opening/expanding/previewing/comparing results never starts Make It Cheaper.
+
+Matched prepared-offer controls explicitly distinguish selection behavior from
+real evaluator acceptance. Canonical source/evaluator controls use existing
+1-QB/K/DEF and Superflex disposable publications. Phone/browser controls exercise
+explicit Generate, two offers, preview/adoption, comparison, keyboard, touch
+emulation and reload. Existing cross-generation, protection, Custom-method,
+ownership and league-switch controls remain mandatory. Public evidence contains
+no owner data. Browser emulation does not establish physical iPhone/Safari or
+live owner acceptance. Exact final validation and deployment receipts are
+published separately; this document does not assert an unfinished gate passed.
+
+No source provider, store, runtime owner, optimizer, Trade/FOIS policy, scoring,
+submitted lineup, preference, 2 GiB cap, 16x restoration allowance or FOIS/Trade
+reservation changes.
+
+
+Validation recovery: the first exact-source full local run encountered two existing Rebuild browser timeouts after real capacity deferral. One admission had 394,358,784 usable bytes against 402,653,184 required. Six earlier gates passed; the already-failed remainder was deliberately interrupted, so regression and the three later gates were not complete. No OOM occurred. A planned two-method matched fresh-container control completed with and without explicit collection; it recovered unreachable retired-fixture objects at setup boundaries, but did not demonstrate a lower overall peak or prove the original objects responsible. The shared browser fixture now collects only unreachable prior-fixture cycles before constructing its normal fixture/viewport and reports process/container measurements. GC stays enabled; every real search, exclusion, viewport, timeout and assertion remains. Admission, reserves and application cleanup are unchanged. Final-source full local and hosted validation remain mandatory.
